### Phase 17: Security Testing

### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api/v1
@accessToken = your_access_token_here
@maliciousOrigin = https://evil-site.com

### ============================================
### 1. Rate Limiting Tests
### ============================================

### Test 1.1: Auth Rate Limiter (should block after 5 attempts)
# Run this multiple times rapidly (10+)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "wrongpassword"
}

###

### Test 1.2: Password Reset Rate Limiter (should block after 3 attempts per hour)
# Run this 4 times
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@example.com"
}

###

### Test 1.3: Search Rate Limiter (should block after 30 per minute)
# Run this 35 times rapidly
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?q=test

###

### Test 1.4: Review Rate Limiter (should block after 5 per hour)
# First, login and get a token, then run this 6 times
POST {{baseUrl}}/reviews
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": "clx123456789",
  "rating": 5,
  "comment": "Test review"
}

###

### ============================================
### 2. XSS Protection Tests
### ============================================

### Test 2.1: XSS in Registration (should sanitize)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "xss@test.com",
  "password": "Test1234!",
  "firstName": "<script>alert('XSS')</script>",
  "lastName": "<img src=x onerror=alert('XSS')>",
  "phone": "+251912345678"
}

###

### Test 2.2: XSS in Product Search (should sanitize)
GET {{baseUrl}}/products?search=<script>alert('XSS')</script>

###

### Test 2.3: XSS in Review Comment (should sanitize)
POST {{baseUrl}}/reviews
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": "clx123456789",
  "rating": 5,
  "comment": "Great product! <script>steal_cookies()</script>"
}

###

### ============================================
### 3. SQL Injection Tests
### ============================================

### Test 3.1: SQL Injection in Search (should detect and log)
GET {{baseUrl}}/products?search=test' UNION SELECT * FROM users--

###

### Test 3.2: SQL Injection in Filter (should detect and log)
GET {{baseUrl}}/products?category=vegetables' OR '1'='1

###

### Test 3.3: SQL Injection in Order By (should detect and log)
GET {{baseUrl}}/products?sortBy=price; DROP TABLE products;--

###

### ============================================
### 4. Path Traversal Tests
### ============================================

### Test 4.1: Path Traversal in File Access (should detect and log)
GET {{baseUrl}}/uploads/../../../etc/passwd

###

### Test 4.2: Path Traversal in Product Image (should detect and log)
GET {{baseUrl}}/products?image=..\..\..\..\windows\system32\config\sam

###

### ============================================
### 5. Authentication & Authorization Tests
### ============================================

### Test 5.1: Access Protected Route Without Token (should return 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/cart

###

### Test 5.2: Access Protected Route With Invalid Token (should return 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/cart
Authorization: Bearer invalid_token_here

###

### Test 5.3: Access Admin Route as Buyer (should return 403)
# First login as buyer, then:
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/analytics/overview
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###

### Test 5.4: Access Seller Route as Buyer (should return 403)
# First login as buyer, then:
GET {{baseUrl}}/seller/analytics/overview
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###

### ============================================
### 6. CORS Tests
### ============================================

### Test 6.1: Request from Malicious Origin (should be rejected)
# This test requires a browser or tool that sends Origin header
GET {{baseUrl}}/products
Origin: {{maliciousOrigin}}

###

### Test 6.2: Preflight Request from Malicious Origin (should be rejected)
OPTIONS {{baseUrl}}/products
Origin: {{maliciousOrigin}}
Access-Control-Request-Method: GET

###

### ============================================
### 7. Input Validation Tests
### ============================================

### Test 7.1: Invalid Email Format (should return validation error)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "Test1234!",
  "firstName": "John",
  "lastName": "Doe",
  "phone": "+251912345678"
}

###

### Test 7.2: Weak Password (should return validation error)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "weak@test.com",
  "password": "weak",
  "firstName": "John",
  "lastName": "Doe",
  "phone": "+251912345678"
}

###

### Test 7.3: Invalid Phone Format (should return validation error)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "phone@test.com",
  "password": "Test1234!",
  "firstName": "John",
  "lastName": "Doe",
  "phone": "123"
}

###

### Test 7.4: Invalid Product Data (should return validation error)
POST {{baseUrl}}/products
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "price": -100,
  "stockQuantity": "not-a-number"
}

###

### ============================================
### 8. Password Security Tests
### ============================================

### Test 8.1: Common Password (should be rejected if validation added)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "common@test.com",
  "password": "Password123!",
  "firstName": "John",
  "lastName": "Doe",
  "phone": "+251912345678"
}

###

### Test 8.2: Password Reset Token Expiry (should fail after 1 hour)
# First request reset:
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@example.com"
}

# Wait 1+ hour, then try to reset:
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "expired_token_here",
  "newPassword": "NewTest1234!"
}

###

### ============================================
### 9. File Upload Security Tests
### ============================================

### Test 9.1: Upload Executable File (should be rejected)
# Note: This requires a file upload endpoint
POST {{baseUrl}}/products
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----WebKitFormBoundary

------WebKitFormBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="image"; filename="malicious.exe"
Content-Type: application/x-msdownload

[Binary content here]
------WebKitFormBoundary--

###

### Test 9.2: Upload Oversized File (should be rejected - over 5MB)
# This test requires actual large file upload

###

### Test 9.3: Upload PHP Script Disguised as Image (should be rejected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/products
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----WebKitFormBoundary

------WebKitFormBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="image"; filename="script.php"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

<?php system($_GET['cmd']); ?>
------WebKitFormBoundary--

###

### ============================================
### 10. JWT Security Tests
### ============================================

### Test 10.1: Use Expired Access Token (should return 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/cart
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJzdWIiOiIxMjM0NTY3ODkwIiwiZXhwIjoxNTE2MjM5MDIyfQ.expired

###

### Test 10.2: Refresh Token Reuse (should fail if rotation implemented)
# First refresh:
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "your_refresh_token"
}

# Try to use same refresh token again:
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "your_refresh_token"
}

###

### Test 10.3: Tampered JWT Token (should return 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/cart
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.tampered_payload.tampered_signature

###

### ============================================
### 11. Error Handling Tests
### ============================================

### Test 11.1: Server Error Should Not Leak Info (should not show stack trace)
GET {{baseUrl}}/nonexistent-endpoint-that-causes-error

###

### Test 11.2: Database Error Should Not Leak Schema (should return generic error)
# Try to access non-existent resource
GET {{baseUrl}}/products/invalid-id-format

###

### ============================================
### 12. Suspicious Activity Tests
### ============================================

### Test 12.1: Bot User Agent (should be logged)
GET {{baseUrl}}/products
User-Agent: BadBot/1.0

###

### Test 12.2: Multiple Suspicious Patterns (should be logged)
GET {{baseUrl}}/products?search=<script>alert('xss')</script>' UNION SELECT * FROM users--&category=../../../etc/passwd

###

### Test 12.3: Rapid Requests from Same IP (should be logged)
# Run this 200 times rapidly:
GET {{baseUrl}}/products

###

### ============================================
### 13. Security Headers Tests
### ============================================

### Test 13.1: Check Security Headers (should include HSTS, CSP, etc.)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

# Expected headers:
# Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
# X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
# X-Frame-Options: DENY
# X-XSS-Protection: 1; mode=block
# Content-Security-Policy: ...

###

### ============================================
### 14. Session Management Tests
### ============================================

### Test 14.1: Concurrent Sessions (should allow multiple sessions)
# Login from two different devices/browsers
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "Test1234!"
}

###

### Test 14.2: Logout Should Invalidate Token (client-side only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

# Try to use token after logout:
GET {{baseUrl}}/cart
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###

### ============================================
### 15. Business Logic Security Tests
### ============================================

### Test 15.1: Negative Quantity in Cart (should be rejected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/cart
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": "clx123456789",
  "quantity": -5
}

###

### Test 15.2: Order Someone Else's Cart (should fail)
# Try to checkout with another user's cart ID
POST {{baseUrl}}/checkout
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "addressId": "clx123456789",
  "paymentMethod": "CASH_ON_DELIVERY",
  "cartId": "another_users_cart_id"
}

###

### Test 15.3: Cancel Someone Else's Order (should fail)
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/another_users_order_id/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Changed my mind"
}

###

### Test 15.4: Review Product Without Purchase (should fail if enforced)
POST {{baseUrl}}/reviews
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": "never_purchased_product_id",
  "rating": 1,
  "comment": "Fake review"
}

###

### ============================================
### 16. Data Exposure Tests
### ============================================

### Test 16.1: User List Should Not Expose Sensitive Data
GET {{baseUrl}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

# Should NOT return: passwords, password hashes, reset tokens, email verification tokens

###

### Test 16.2: Error Messages Should Not Expose Database Structure
GET {{baseUrl}}/products/99999999

# Should NOT return SQL queries, table names, column names

###

